From 988abf6ed2cc0b8a624fc1bf46308d2aa9d90354 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ggbdpq <ggbdpq@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 06:00:33 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] usage: the context map's tiles are read once their rects hold
 still (#3488)

#3488: "chromium de 420px: the context window as a map" failed with
"two tiles overlap" in a GUI run beside a go test, while the file alone
passed three rounds of 11/11. The read was a single look after the
running animations under the open session ended, and that wait can
clear before the map is done laying out: the card's size class (max520,
which draws the map 2:1 against 3.1:1) is set from a requestAnimationFrame
that the cardSizes observer defers, and when the flip lands the map's
own ResizeObserver lays the tiles out again, the kept ones gliding to
their new place over .62s. A read landing in that re-layout sees tiles
mid-move.

The rects are now read the way wheelTo above already waits for the
scroll: looks a hundred ms apart until three in a row read the same,
and the assertions run on that settled look. A settled map that really
overlapped would still fail, and one that never settles still fails on
the last look. Replaying the tilesOf math at both card heights and every
stale crossing between them shows no settled layout of this fixture
overlaps, so the assertions keep their teeth.

Chromium, the whole file: 8 rounds with the busy machine replayed (the
size class flipping right as the read goes out) failed 8/8 as "two
tiles overlap" before, 0/8 after. WebKit unchanged green.

